# HTML Semantic Tags

## 📌 Introduction

Semantic tags in HTML are elements that clearly describe the meaning and purpose of the content they contain.

They help developers write meaningful, well-structured, and readable HTML code.

## 1. What Are Semantic Tags?

**Definition:** Semantic HTML elements are HTML elements that convey the meaning and purpose of their content to browsers, developers, and assistive technologies.

For example:

* `<header>` defines introductory content or a header section.
* `<nav>` defines a section containing navigation links.
* `<main>` represents the main content of a document.
* `<section>` represents a thematic section of content.
* `<article>` represents self-contained content.
* `<footer>` defines footer information for a page or section.

## 2. Types of Semantic Tags

### 1. `<header>`

The `<header>` tag represents introductory content or a header for a page or section.

**Example:**

```html
<header>
    <h1>My Website</h1>
    <p>Welcome to my website!</p>
</header>
```

### 2. `<nav>`

The `<nav>` tag defines a section containing navigation links.

**Example:**

```html
<nav>
    <a href="index.html">Home</a>
    <a href="about.html">About</a>
    <a href="contact.html">Contact</a>
</nav>
```

### 3. `<main>`

The `<main>` tag represents the main content of a document.

**Example:**

```html
<main>
    <h1>About HTML</h1>
    <p>HTML is used to structure web pages.</p>
</main>
```

### 4. `<section>`

The `<section>` tag groups related content into a thematic section.

**Example:**

```html
<section>
    <h2>My Skills</h2>
    <p>I am learning HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.</p>
</section>
```

### 5. `<article>`

The `<article>` tag represents self-contained content that can stand independently, such as a blog post or news article.

**Example:**

```html
<article>
    <h2>My First Blog</h2>
    <p>This is my first blog post.</p>
</article>
```

### 6. `<aside>`

The `<aside>` tag represents content that is indirectly related to the main content, such as a sidebar.

**Example:**

```html
<aside>
    <h3>Related Topics</h3>
    <p>Learn CSS after HTML.</p>
</aside>
```

### 7. `<footer>`

The `<footer>` tag represents footer information for a page or section.

**Example:**

```html
<footer>
    <p>Copyright &copy; 2026 My Website</p>
</footer>
```

### 8. `<figure>` and `<figcaption>`

* `<figure>` represents self-contained content, such as an image or illustration.
* `<figcaption>` provides a caption for the content inside a `<figure>` element.

**Example:**

```html
<figure>
    <img src="flower.jpg" alt="A beautiful flower">
    <figcaption>A beautiful flower.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

## 3. Summary of Semantic Tags

| Tag            | Purpose                                             |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `<header>`     | Defines introductory content or a header            |
| `<nav>`        | Defines navigation links                            |
| `<main>`       | Defines the main content                            |
| `<section>`    | Groups thematically related content                 |
| `<article>`    | Defines self-contained content                      |
| `<aside>`      | Defines indirectly related content                  |
| `<footer>`     | Defines footer information                          |
| `<figure>`     | Represents self-contained content, such as an image |
| `<figcaption>` | Defines a caption for a figure                      |

## 4. Complete HTML Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Semantic HTML</title>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>My Coding Journey</h1>
        <p>Learning HTML step by step.</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <a href="#home">Home</a>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
    </nav>

    <main id="home">

        <section id="about">
            <h2>About Me</h2>
            <p>I am learning web development.</p>
        </section>

        <article>
            <h2>My First HTML Lesson</h2>
            <p>Today, I learned about semantic tags.</p>
        </article>

        <aside>
            <h3>Learning Tip</h3>
            <p>Practice HTML every day.</p>
        </aside>

    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>Copyright &copy; 2026 My Coding Journey</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
```

## 5. Advantages of Semantic Tags

1. **Readability:** Makes HTML code easier to understand.
2. **Accessibility:** Helps assistive technologies interpret page structure.
3. **SEO:** Helps search engines understand the structure and meaning of content.
4. **Maintainability:** Makes code easier to manage and update.
5. **Structure:** Gives different parts of a webpage meaningful roles.

## 🎯 What I Learned

* What semantic HTML tags are.
* The purpose of `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`, and `<footer>`.
* How to structure a webpage using semantic elements.
* The importance of semantic HTML in accessibility, readability, and SEO.

